Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Adult Medicine  CNT  126 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  ELIZABETH A RAFFERTY  M D  Resident  Colleen A Lamb  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 48 year old woman who presents with right breast mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HIGH GRADE  WITH SYNCYTIAL GROWTH PATTERN AND PROMINENT LYMPHOPLASMACYTIC INFILTRATE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy reveal an invasive carcinoma involving five of five core biopsies  The tumor grows in large fused nests with a distinctly syncytial growth pattern  There is a dense inflammatory infiltrate composed predominately of lymphocytes and plasma present  The tumor cells are large and markedly pleomorphic with ill defined cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic vesicular nuclei with marked nuclear contour irregularities and prominent macronucleoli  Scattered mitotic figures including atypical mitoses are readily identified  The morphologic findings are those of a high grade ductal carcinoma and suggest the possibility of a medullary carcinoma  Definite classification is deferred to the excision  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or co